Search by image for DeepSeek Harness

Original work by the dsh-zcode-plugins contributors, MIT licensed.

Not to be confused with the ZCode `image-search` plugin: that one is a hosted
keyword search over a curated collection and needs a ZCode account plus a coding
plan. This plugin searches in the opposite direction — the query is an image —
and needs no account, no API key, and no outbound proxy.

Engine:

- Baidu 识图 (graph.baidu.com). The plugin drives the public web page with a
  real browser: it opens the entry page, hands the query image to the page's
  file input, and reads the recognition phrase, the similar-image grid, and any
  external page links from the rendered result. Baidu publishes no keyless
  reverse-image API, so the page is the interface. Baidu may change its layout,
  rate-limit, or temporarily disable the service; the tool reports what it
  actually saw and never fabricates a match.

Third-party services: the plugin sends only the image the caller supplies. No
credentials, no proxy, and no tracking are configured.
